0..49 Comment "//! A rule of a theory that answers a stuck call."
50..53 Comment "//!"
54..130 Comment "//! The unit rule `band one x <=> x` answers its second argument. Where that"
131..207 Comment "//! argument is `encode b` for a variable `b`, the call does not reduce. The"
208..282 Comment "//! normal form of the term is then that call. A path between the call and"
283..321 Comment "//! the term must hold by reflexivity."
322..325 Comment "//!"
326..399 Comment "//! The checker takes the normal form of the term by the rules first. The"
400..475 Comment "//! kernel does the same. Each then compares the call that the rule answers"
476..512 Comment "//! with the call on the other side."
513..516 Comment "//!"
517..533 Comment "//! - see: #8278"
